le game sliding down the left edge. The game was level at move 15 before F6 cost Opus 5.5 5.3 points, and from move 23 it lost between 5.3 and 7.5 points per move on the B and A files while the engine kept pointing at D2. The 12k also gave back 5.0 to 7.2 points on several of its replies, but Opus 5.5 ended at -12.0 after A8 and never got closer than -11.7. Black resigned with the left side and bottom edge in White's hands.", "moments": [{"turn": 9, "text": "E4 stretches the E-file wall down, but the lead goes from -0.0 to -5.3, a loss of 5.2 points. The engine preferred D6, the point White took next. It was the first big swing in a game that had been level."}, {"turn": 15, "text": "F6 dropped the lead from -0.0 to -5.3, a 5.3-point loss, with E8 as the engine's choice. The 12k took E8 on the next move, losing -0.1 by the numbers, and that top-side point held the game for White until the end."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "B7 is the first of the edge-crawl blunders: -4.4 to -11.5, a 7.2-point loss, with D2 still the engine's choice. The 12k answered C9 and lost 6.7 points, so the lead came back to -4.8. Each side kept giving the points back and forth, but Opus 5.5 kept losing more than it won back."}, {"turn": 31, "text": "A8 is the worst move of Opus 5.5's game, 7.5 points, taking the lead from -4.5 to -12.0. It was the fifth edge move in a row on the left after B8, B7, B6 and B9. The engine wanted D2 at the bottom instead, where the bottom row was still open."}, {"turn": 32, "text": "E2 matches the engine's first choice and loses -0.1 by the numbers. It shuts the bottom edge for White, and from here the lead stays around -12.0 to -11.7 through the late moves. The final board shows White's group across the left and centre, with 10 Black stones captured, and Opus 5.5 resigned."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py and count.py only parse a pasted board and compute group liberties and area counts of the current position, with no candidate loops or lookahead; the other commands only read and append to notes (CLAUDE.md, games.md).", "stop": false}}